OL,3,GNEWSANuclear test veteran calls for
OL,4,A'truth and justice'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA nuclear test veteran says he hopes an
OL,7,Fupcoming government investigation into
OL,8,Fthe health legacy of Britain's Cold
OL,9,FWar-era atomic programme will give
OL,10,F"truth and justice" to those affected.
OL,12,FCapt Terry Hughes, of the Forest of
OL,13,FDean, Gloucestershire, was 19 when he
OL,14,Fwas sent to Christmas Island in the
OL,15,FPacific, where nuclear bombs were
OL,16,Fdetonated in tests. He has suffered a
OL,17,Frange of health problems since.
OL,19,FIn the 1950s and 60s, 22,000 servicemen
OL,20,Fwere sent to Australia and the South
OL,21,FPacific to help test the nuclear bombs.
